concurrentPublishSamePlanWithRestriction: 4 threads, same requestKey+operator. Outcomes: OK or 409 (PLAN_STATE_CONFLICT). Assert: at least one OK; final plan PUBLISHED; rearrange count == 1; version == 2. This verifies "同一计划的并发改签和重排不得产生两套生效时刻".

Hmm wait — actually could a loser thread enter tx BEFORE winner commits and both compute shift and both try insert idempotency → DuplicateKeyException → resolveDuplicate → replay returns winner's response → OK. Or loser waits on publish lock → sees PUBLISHED → 409. Either way fine. Assert outcomes are OK-or-409, exactly one rearrange.

For concurrent reschedule same old plan: two threads reschedule(O→N1) and reschedule(O→N2). Both acquire publish lock serially. First commits: O CANCELLED, N1 PUBLISHED. Second: loads O FOR UPDATE → status CANCELLED → 409 PLAN_STATE_CONFLICT. Assert exactly one OK; final: exactly one of N1/N2 published; one effective set of times; rearrange records total == number of shifted winners (1 if winner needed shift).

