Getting messy; simpler to build with ObjectMapper / ObjectNode. Use objectMapper.createObjectNode(). That's cleaner:

```java
private String createJson(String reqKey, String restKey, String section, String start, String end, Integer speed) {
    ObjectNode n = objectMapper.createObjectNode();
    n.put("requestKey", reqKey); n.put("restrictionKey", restKey);
    if (section != null) n.put("sectionId", section);
    if (start != null) n.put("startUtc", start);
    if (end != null) n.put("endUtc", end);
    if (speed != null) n.put("maxSpeedKmh", speed);
    n.put("operator", "op-test");
    return n.toString();
}
